// NOTE: When I return to this, it's worth breaking up a yarn project for each "chapter" of the game.
// We can use this namespacing convention epending on the phases of that chapter, since it may not be consistent across chapters

title: Brewing_Chapter1
---
<<declare $is_served = false>>
<<declare $is_pref = true>>
===

// TODO: Loop this based on the dialogue
title: Brewing_Chapter1_OldMan
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Old Man: Welcome into my tea shop, {$name}! I'm glad the world brought us together
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Old Man: Just the kick I wanted, thank you!
<<else>>
    Old Man: Not quite, green tea please! // doesn't loop yet
<<endif>>
===

// I was planning on just a generic character here, but she could work
title: Brewing_Chapter1_Mercenary
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Miranda: May as well get something while I'm here...
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Miranda: Just what I needed after a tedious job.
    // TODO: Pass along is pref and have another option when it isn't the pref 
    // TODO: If I keep Miranda, we can use "is pref" depending on what's served. Just two for now, but neither is "bad"?
    // I guess we'll want the freedom for more in the future, but that is not in the prototype scope
<<else>>
    Miranda: Not quite... hopefully I'm not up all night.
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter1_Forg
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Forg: I just lost my race! {$name}, can I get some of that tea I had last time? That gave me extra energy?
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Forg: Haha!! I can feel it already... Sambo's goin' down!
<<else>>
    Forg: Tastes... different... but does it work? ONE WAY TO FIND OUT!
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter1_General
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    General: Good day, Tea Seller! I am passing through with my troops, and we humbly request your FINEST teas! You must aid your fief and provide us health and strength!
    General: Please, Tea Seller, aid us with something that will provide stamina for the journey ahead!
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    General: Brilliant, thank you Tea Seller! Continue to aid my soldiers.
<<else>>
    Character: My teas are too strong for you, General...
    General: Not quite what I had in mind... but alas. Please, aid my soldiers!
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter1_SoldierHurt
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Hurt Soldier: Ugh... I feel nauseous...
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Hurt Soldier: Whoa! What an instant effect!
<<else>>
    Hurt Soldier: Hmm... that helps a bit... I think I need the bathroom...
<<endif>>
===

title: Brewing_Chapter1_SoldierFine
---
<<if $is_served == false>>
    Soldier: Give me something to strengthen me for the battles ahead- like a nice breakfast that sets me up for the day!
<<elseif $is_served == true and $is_pref == true>>
    Soldier: I...
    Soldier: AM A WARRIOR!!!!
<<else>>
    Soldier: I'm sure this will kick in eventually...
<<endif>>
===

